{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-f788dd72-a75f-499c-8ae2-a51738fc807f-2\nfc_01e9371c-e302-97f8-af70-8761aa31ecbf_2","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/Users/psudokit/.claude/skills/explore-codebase/SKILL.md"},"result":{"success":{"content":"---\nname: explore-codebase\ndescription: >\n  Quickly map an unfamiliar codebase — entry points, architecture, key modules, data flow,\n  and conventions — before making changes. Use when the user says \"explore this repo\",\n  \"how does this codebase work\", \"give me a tour\", \"where is X handled\", \"understand this\n  project\", \"I just cloned this\", or is new to a repo and needs orientation before editing.\n---\n\n# Explore Codebase\n\nBuild an accurate mental model of a repo fast, then report a concise map — not a file dump.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. **Orient.** Read `README`, `package.json`/`pyproject.toml`/`go.mod`, `CLAUDE.md`, and any\n   `docs/`. Identify language(s), framework, and how the project is built/run/tested.\n2. **Find entry points.** `main`, `index`, server bootstrap, CLI entry, route registration.\n3. **Map the layers.** Group directories by role: routes/controllers, services/domain, data/models,\n   UI/components, config, tests. Note the dependency direction between them.\n4. **Trace one real path** end-to-end (e.g. one request or one command) to see how layers connect.\n5. **Capture conventions.** Naming, error handling, state management, test style, lint/format rules.\n6. **Report** (see format). Prefer `path:line` references so the user can click through.\n\n## Report format\n\n```md\n## <Repo> — map\n**Stack:** <langs/frameworks> · **Run:** <cmd> · **Test:** <cmd>\n\n**Architecture:** <1-2 sentences on the shape>\n\n**Key areas**\n- `src/<...>` — <role>\n- ...\n\n**One flow:** <entry> → <service> → <data> (with path:line refs)\n\n**Conventions worth knowing:** <naming, errors, tests, gotchas>\n\n**Where to start for <the user's goal>:** <specific files>\n```\n\n## Rules\n\n- Use fan-out search (Grep/Glob) over reading whole files; read excerpts to confirm.\n- For large repos, spawn parallel **Explore** agents per subsystem and synthesize their findings.\n- Don't guess architecture from names alone — confirm with a real trace before asserting it.\n","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":49,"fileSize":1968,"path":"/Users/psudokit/.claude/skills/explore-codebase/SKILL.md","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":49},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-f788dd72-a75f-499c-8ae2-a51738fc807f-2\nfc_01e9371c-e302-97f8-af70-8761aa31ecbf_2","startedAtMs":"1789791253403","completedAtMs":"1789791254254"},"model_call_id":"f4af69a3-9b8b-4f21-b178-255e9d653d4e-0-9qmx","session_id":"75e0984d-df8c-4329-aadc-033e626c8ad6","timestamp_ms":1789791254786}
